    "body": "Rejecting with NotAllowedError due to lack of system-level permission increases fingerprinting risk. Typically, enumeration APIs should simply return an empty list when permission is not granted so that applications cannot deduce the permission state.\n\nTo resolve the Android issue I think we will need to modify the browser implementation to trigger the system permission flow automatically (without user activation) when an origin with policy-granted HID permissions calls getDevices or registers HID connection event listeners. I think we should keep the current behavior (return empty list immediately) and then fire connection events for any devices discovered after the system permission is granted rather than blocking until the permission flow is completed or aborted.",
